# MagicSpells Workspace Overview

## Mode fork (choose first)

| Mode | Triggers | Do |
|------|----------|-----|
| **Plugin** | Java, new/`spell-class` types, config API keys, wiki docs for the plugin, Gradle/build | Edit `MagicSpells/` (+ wiki when surface changes). Follow **wiki-documentation** and **unit-tests** rules. |
| **Script** | Gameplay YAML packs, LoM content, `Ms_Scripts`, `MagicSpells_Scripting`, `spells-*` pack folders | Edit packs only. Follow **scripts-authoring** (rules stay in this workspace; packs are not a git repo). Do not change plugin Java or shipped defaults unless the user asks. |

Same chat may switch modes when the user does. If both are needed, finish the active mode’s done-criteria before crossing.

## Layout

Multi-root / multi-repo (not a monorepo):

| Path | Repo | Branch | Role |
|------|------|--------|------|
| `MagicSpells/` | `Team-Sneakymouse/MagicSpells` | `DvZ` | Plugin source (PaperMC) |
| `MagicSpells.wiki/` | `Team-Sneakymouse/MagicSpells.wiki` | `master` | GitHub wiki clone |
| `Ms_Scripts/` → `../MagicSpells_Scripting/` | (local files only, not a git repo) | — | LoM gameplay YAML (gitignored symlink) |

### Branch roles (`MagicSpells/` / `origin`)

LoM mainline is **`origin/DvZ`** (not GitHub `main`, not `upstream`).

| Role | Typical name | Publishes to sneakyrp? |
|------|--------------|------------------------|
| **Live** | `DvZ` | Yes when `publish.yml` points here (production-ish) |
| **Milestone** | e.g. `feature/cast-item-spelldata` | Yes while that branch is listed in `publish.yml` — feeds the **dev** server for a testing phase |
| **Feature** | other `feature/*` | No — merge into the active milestone (or `DvZ`) when ready |

Source of truth for which branch auto-publishes: `MagicSpells/.github/workflows/publish.yml` (`on.push.branches`). Changing that filter: merge current publish/Gradle surface from `DvZ` into the new publisher first (shaded `plugin` publication + `gradle/verify-publications.gradle`), then flip the filter. Day-to-day feature pushes should not publish.

If the user says “feature branch” / “pull DvZ into my branch” without naming it: state the current checkout and ask before merge/stash/push.

`upstream` (`TheComputerGeek2/MagicSpells`) is only for occasional sync-from-upstream; ignore it for LoM merge/publish work.

## Source map (`MagicSpells/`) — plugin mode

- **Gradle multi-project** — root `settings.gradle.kts`; build with `./gradlew build` from `MagicSpells/` (or from the workspace root — `./gradlew` there forwards into `MagicSpells/`).
- **Test server** — `./gradlew runServer` starts a Paper 1.21.4 server with the shaded `:core` plugin (`xyz.jpenilla.run-paper`; server files under `core/run/`).
- **`:core`** — main plugin. Java packages stay `com.nisovin.magicspells`; Maven coords use `io.github.team-sneakymouse`.
- **Spell classes** — `core/src/main/java/com/nisovin/magicspells/spells/`
  - Categories: `instant/`, `targeted/`, `buff/`, `command/`, `passive/`, plus top-level general spells
  - YAML `spell-class` is relative to the spells package, e.g. `.instant.ConjureSpell`
- **Spell effects** — `.../spelleffects/` (`SpellEffect.java`, `effecttypes/`)
- **Config helpers** — `.../util/config/` (`ConfigData`, `getConfigData*` on spells)
- **Default YAMLs** — `core/src/main/resources/` (`general.yml`, `mana.yml`, `spells-*.yml`, …) — shipped defaults only, not LoM packs
- **Extensions** — `:shop`, `:factions`, `:memory`, `:teams`, `:towny`
- **NMS** — `:nms:shared`, `:nms:v1_21_4` (version modules; see README)

## Docs map

- Community / fork wiki files live in **`MagicSpells.wiki/`** (Markdown). Live site: https://github.com/Team-Sneakymouse/MagicSpells/wiki
- **Spell YAML entrypoint (both modes):** `MagicSpells.wiki/Agent-Guide.md` → `Spell-List.md` (one-liners) → feature page; patterns in `Spell-Cookbook.md` / `Spell-Anti-Patterns.md`
- Skim indexes: `Spell-Effects.md`, `Modifier-Condition-List.md`, `Passive-Trigger-List.md`, `Variables.md`; machine maps: `spell-index.json`, `effect-index.json`, `modifier-condition-index.json`
- Regenerate indexes: `python3 scripts/wiki/generate-all.py` (canonical tooling under `scripts/wiki/`; wiki `scripts/` wrappers forward here)
- Conventions: `MagicSpells.wiki/Wiki-Conventions.md`
- CI: `.github/workflows/wiki-docs.yml` (workspace) and `MagicSpells/.github/workflows/wiki-docs.yml`
- Official upstream wiki (do not treat as this fork’s source of truth): https://github.com/TheComputerGeek2/MagicSpells/wiki
- Quick config object notes in-repo: `MagicSpells/MagicSpells Config Objects.md`
- Build/publish details: `MagicSpells/README.md`

## Agent habits

- Treat `MagicSpells/` and `MagicSpells.wiki/` as **independent git histories** (commits, pushes, PRs stay in the repo you changed). Pack YAML is **not** part of those histories.
- After a merge the user did not ask to push: say it is local-only, or sync locals to `origin` before switching branches — do not leave unpushed merges unexplained.
- Prefer reading an existing similar spell/effect (and its wiki page) before inventing patterns.
- **Plugin mode:** wiki-documentation + unit-tests rules; `SpellSnippetValidator` for YAML surface checks; test on `runServer` via `MagicSpells/core/run/plugins/MagicSpells/spells-test.yml` or new `spells-*.yml` there (gitignored `**/run/`). Leave `core/src/main/resources/` alone unless changing shipped defaults.
- **Script mode:** follow `scripts-authoring.mdc`; use wiki as reference only; test packs on `runServer` without committing them into the plugin repo.
- Warning-migration live checklist: `MagicSpells/MANUAL-TEST-WARNING-MIGRATION.md` + fixtures in `spells-warning-migration.yml` (`wm_*`).
